# Day 23 - 30 Days Python Challenge 🐍

## What I Learned Today
- Multithreading (`threading`, `ThreadPoolExecutor`)
- Solution walkthrough of the previous exercise

## Programs Written

### 1. Word Counter
A program that counts words in all `.txt` files inside a folder concurrently
using `ThreadPoolExecutor`, instead of processing files one by one.

### 2. Heist Simulation
A mini heist game where 4 crew members (Hacker, Lockpicker, Explosives Expert,
Driver) each attempt their task simultaneously using `threading.Thread`, with
`t.join()` ensuring all threads complete before declaring mission success or
failure.

## Concepts Covered
- Multithreading with the `threading` module
- Concurrent execution using `ThreadPoolExecutor`
- `thread.start()` and `thread.join()`
- Random-chance based task simulation

